Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["\<\
Mathematica code for implementation of the model for different cooperative \
ecological phenomena\
\>", "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.980838801682358*^9, 3.980838821219701*^9}, {
  3.9808392557478*^9, 3.980839259530222*^9}, {3.98894452928913*^9, 
  3.988944536398575*^9}, {4.000550050057602*^9, 4.000550069183681*^9}, {
  4.000550665677516*^9, 4.00055067444103*^9}, {4.000552217701892*^9, 
  4.000552229070952*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6d7aafff-7961-4ba7-a807-\
81ec92c0d9b2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This notebook contains source code for the following preprint article:\n",
 StyleBox["\nDroste MJ, Planqu\[EAcute] R, Bruggeman FJ (2026) Emergent \
metabolic cooperation in communities of microbes that maximise growth rate by \
optimal protein expression. \n",
  FontWeight->"Bold"]
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9296947437186413`*^9, 3.9296951020392857`*^9}, {
   3.9301480170576887`*^9, 3.930148041336217*^9}, {3.930217504016037*^9, 
   3.930217657615096*^9}, {3.930217693247149*^9, 3.930217726206396*^9}, {
   3.9433578287223663`*^9, 3.9433578377303247`*^9}, {3.9488647433446007`*^9, 
   3.948864937179102*^9}, {3.948865021276495*^9, 3.948865021678293*^9}, 
   3.948865127850287*^9, {3.966665356685046*^9, 3.9666653768499613`*^9}, 
   3.966665977467705*^9, {3.992920968059231*^9, 3.992920976301819*^9}, {
   4.00055009951343*^9, 4.000550117571023*^9}, {4.002098761747344*^9, 
   4.0020987677759027`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0264e0bf-6735-4b2c-aa13-\
8a47a1711817"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Short description",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\nThis code contains the implementation of the models for different \
cooperative ecological phenomena discussed in the article. For each \
phenomenon, we implement a variant of the growth rate maximisation problem \
that compares the growth rate of two different microbial populations. Since \
each phenomenon is described by a different reaction network and/or parameter \
regime, we define a different set of parameters and an optimisation problem \
for each phenomenon. In all cases, a varying independent parameter results in \
a change in either the optimal community composition, the optimal metabolic \
strategy, or both. More information on the models for different cooperative \
ecological phenomena can be found in the Supplementary Appendices of the \
article.\n\n",
 StyleBox["Note",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.93, 0.27, 0.27]],
 ": In some of the numerical solutions of the optimisations, numerical errors \
appear regarding convergence failure within a set number of iterations. The \
authors have checked that these errors arise because of the independency of \
the optimization problem on some of the variables in certain regimes. For \
instance, whenever mode 2 is the optimal solution, the enzyme and metabolite \
concentrations appearing in mode 1 can take any value within the feasible \
solution space without affecting the optimal solution. This sometimes results \
in a convergence failure. Since we want to use the optimisation problems to \
describe all these different regimes and these errors do not arise from \
numerical instabilities, we have decided to retain to the current algorithms \
and ignore these errors. This however also means that some of the results for \
mode 2 exclusively should be corrected: the growth rate of species B will \
become zero in this case, even though the optimisation will sometimes give a \
random value (as this does not affect the optimisation). Wherever necessary, \
we correct the simulation results by setting the growth rate of the consumer \
to zero explicitly when only mode 2 is used."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->CompressedData["
